# URL of the statcmd Cloudflare Worker's render route (worker/statcmd.js, the
# `/v3` endpoint). This is the base the customizer puts into every generated
# `$(urlfetch …)` command AND the URL the live chat preview fetches to render.
# It's a public URL, not a secret. For the deployed site set a GitHub Actions
# repository variable named VITE_STATCMD_URL; copy this file to `.env.local` for
# local dev (e.g. point it at `http://localhost:8787/v3` while running
# `wrangler dev`). When left blank the customizer falls back to
# https://statcmd.kapkit.ca/v3 for the command string and shows a sample line in
# the preview instead of calling a Worker.
VITE_STATCMD_URL=

# Optional: Mixpanel analytics (see src/shared/analytics.ts). Create a free
# project at https://mixpanel.com, then paste its "Project Token" (Settings →
# Project Settings → Access Keys) here. When set, the customizer loads Mixpanel
# (cookie-based, gated behind the consent banner); leave blank to disable
# analytics entirely (the app works fine without it). The project token is a
# public, write-only identifier, not a secret. For the deployed site set a
# GitHub Actions repository variable named VITE_MIXPANEL_TOKEN.
#
# NOTE: only the Project *Token* goes here. Never put your Mixpanel *API Secret*
# in this file or the bundle — it is a server-side credential and this app ships
# to the browser.
#
# MULTIPLE SITES: Mixpanel's free plan allows unlimited projects, so give each
# site its own project and its own VITE_MIXPANEL_TOKEN. (If you'd rather pool
# several sites into one project, set VITE_MIXPANEL_SITE below instead.)
VITE_MIXPANEL_TOKEN=
# Mixpanel API host — match your project's data-residency region:
# https://api.mixpanel.com (US, the default) or https://api-eu.mixpanel.com (EU).
# Set as a repository variable named VITE_MIXPANEL_HOST for the deployed site.
# Optionally point it at a reverse-proxy subdomain of your own domain to dodge
# ad blockers.
VITE_MIXPANEL_HOST=
# Optional per-site label, only useful when several sites SHARE ONE Mixpanel
# project: it is attached to every event as a `site` super property so you can
# break your reports down by site. Leave blank when each site has its own
# project. Set as a repository variable named VITE_MIXPANEL_SITE.
VITE_MIXPANEL_SITE=
